{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>They</b> — to oppose, because of two: if they do not testify, they shall not spend the night."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is extremely compressed; 'testify' is an inference for ישבעו (literally 'swear'), but the context of Psalms 59:16 and the legal requirement of two witnesses suggests this is the intended sense. The word לא־ישרת is textually difficult and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:18.499648112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}